// 2026-10-19 (contract tiers, plan 2026-10-19-contract-tiers-and-regularity.md):
// the call-site contract gate's rollout stage. allow = migration stage (the
// gate computes verdicts, rejects nothing); warn = each refuted/unproven site
// announces on stderr; deny = the Option-1 end state (refuted and unproven
// contracted call sites are compile errors).
//
// FLIP CRITERIA (the end of the stdlib contract migration, censused
// 2026-10-19 at 90 contracted fns / 23,117 sites across the sweep):
//   1. every stdlib contract is either leverage-carrying (callers prove it)
//      or removed as noise (length/cast/intrinsic sign restatements);
//   2. genuinely dynamic boundaries return Result (the ws_decode idiom);
//   3. the full sweep + suite + harness are green under `policy: warn`
//      with zero announcements — then flip to deny.
// 2026-10-20: FLIPPED. The sweep reached zero announcements under `warn`
// (materially sooner than the original estimate), so this file now carries
// the active `deny` row. For a migration experiment, override with
// `policy: warn;` in a temporary config; do not omit the row (that installs
// the inactive `allow` default).

policy: deny;
